==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*hlaibaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*kel-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*kley-}}.  Cognate with Old High German {{term|hleib|lang=goh}} (German {{term|Laib|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|hleifr|lang=non}} (Icelandic {{term|hleifur||loaf|lang=is}}, Old Swedish ''lēver''), Gothic {{term|𐌷𐌻𐌰𐌹𐍆𐍃|tr=hlaifs|lang=got}}.  The Indo-European root is also the source of Ancient Greek {{term|κλίβανος||baking oven|tr=klibanos|lang=grc}}, Proto-Slavic {{m|sla-pro|*xlěbъ}} (Russian {{term|хлеб||bread|lang=ru}}, Polish {{term|chleb||bread|lang=pl}}).

